  {
   "id": "ID_2024_CLASS_FEATURE_RANGER_FAVORED_ENEMY",
   "name": "Favored Enemy",
   "type": "Class Feature",
   "source": "SRD 5.2.1",
   "ruleset": "dnd2024",
   "description": "<p>You always have the Hunter’s Mark spell prepared. You can cast it twice without expending a spell slot, and you regain all expended uses of this ability when you finish a Long Rest.</p>\n<p>The number of times you can cast the spell without a spell slot increases when you reach certain Ranger levels, as shown in the Favored Enemy column of the Ranger Features table.</p>",
   "rules": [
    {
     "kind": "grant_spell",
     "spell": "ID_2024_SPELL_HUNTERS_MARK",
     "mode": "always_prepared",
     "counts_against_prepared": false,
     "spell_list": "Ranger",
     "free_cast": {
      "uses": {
       "type": "table",
       "key": "favored_enemy"
      },
      "recharge": "long_rest"
     },
     "also_with_slots": true
    }
   ],
   "data": {
    "class": "Ranger",
    "level": 1
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ID_2024_CLASS_FEATURE_RANGER_WEAPON_MASTERY",
   "name": "Weapon Mastery",
   "type": "Class Feature",
   "source": "SRD 5.2.1",
   "ruleset": "dnd2024",
   "description": "<p>Your training with weapons allows you to use the mastery properties of two kinds of weapons of your choice with which you have proficiency, such as Longbows and Shortswords.</p>\n<p>Whenever you finish a Long Rest, you can change the kinds of weapons you chose. For example, you could switch to using the mastery properties of Scimitars and Longswords.</p>",
   "rules": [
    {
     "kind": "weapon_mastery",
     "name": "Weapon Mastery",
     "count": {
      "type": "fixed",
      "value": 2
     },
     "filter": {
      "weapon_kind": "any",
      "proficient": true
     },
     "change_on": "long_rest"
    }
   ],
   "data": {
    "class": "Ranger",
    "level": 1
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "ID_2024_CLASS_FEATURE_RANGER_DEFT_EXPLORER",
   "name": "Deft Explorer",
   "type": "Class Feature",
   "source": "SRD 5.2.1",
   "ruleset": "dnd2024",
   "description": "<p>Thanks to your travels, you gain the following benefits.</p>\n<p><b>Expertise.</b> Choose one of your skill proficiencies with which you lack Expertise. You gain Expertise in that skill.</p>\n<p><b>Languages.</b> You know two languages of your choice from the language tables in “Character Creation.”</p>",
   "rules": [
    {
     "kind": "expertise",
     "count": 1,
     "from": "proficient skills without Expertise"
    },
    {
     "kind": "select",
     "type": "Language",
     "name": "Deft Explorer Languages",
     "number": 2,
     "supports": "Standard||Rare"
    }
   ],
   "data": {
    "class": "Ranger",
    "level": 2
   }
  },
  {
